# Recommended additions to your .gitignore when using richardbot-template.
# Copy these lines (or merge with your existing .gitignore).
# Pick a side on each commented option based on your team\'s preference.

# ── Always ignore ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Subprocess dispatch verdicts (runtime, may contain transient info)
.dispatch-out/

# Lease state — runtime data, not source. Keep the dir via .gitkeep.
.claude/state/leases/*.json
!.claude/state/leases/.gitkeep

# Audit log (large, append-only; you may prefer to keep this — pick one)
# .richardbot-memory/_audit.jsonl

# ── Decide per-team ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Memory directory: COMMIT if you want shared institutional memory across the team.
# IGNORE if memory should stay per-developer.
# Default recommendation: COMMIT. Postmortems and friction notes are most valuable
# when the whole team sees them next time the same shape recurs.
# .richardbot-memory/

# ── Anti-patterns — do NOT commit ─────────────────────────────────────────
# These are common accident classes; explicit exclusion prevents foot-guns.
*.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.aws/credentials
